Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w3","rationale":"inverse-error weights on the reduced, less correlated pool4"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and errors are correlated, but the best single models vary across horizons; a per‑horizon best‑model weighting on the stable pool1 may capture that variation.  
Action: weights_best_per_horizon  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current best uses a robust median; try a weighted scheme that still respects model quality but reduces variance by shrinking towards uniform weights on the stable pool1.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.5}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and many models are correlated; a forward‑selection weight that adapts to each horizon may capture complementary strengths better than a static inverse‑error weight.  
Action: weights_forward  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","max_steps":20,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The ranking is unstable and many models are correlated; a forward‑selection pool from the reduced pool4 may give a more diverse set of models, and weighted combination on that pool could improve over the current median pool1 leader.  
Action: select_forward  
Action Input: {"max_steps":20, "metric":"rmse"}

Thought: The current best is a robust median on a small stable pool. To see if a data‑driven meta‑model can improve, try a cross‑series meta‑model weight on the same pool.  
Action: weights_meta_model  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool1","scope":"dataset","metric":"smape"}

Thought: Trimmed mean with a smaller trim (0.1) on the stable pool1 may reduce influence of the worst model while keeping more information, potentially improving over the 0.2 trim.

Action: evaluate_strategy

Action Input: {"combine":"trimmed_mean","pool":"pool1","trim_pct":0.1,"rationale":"test tighter trimming on the stable pool"}

Thought: The top three models have the lowest errors and may dominate; a simple mean of them could outperform the robust median on pool1.  
Action: select_top_k  
Action Input: {"k":3,"metric":"rmse"}

Thought: Try a simple inverse‑error weighting on the very small, low‑error pool6 to see if a focused weighted mean beats the robust median.  
Action: weights_inverse_error  
Action Input: {"pool":"pool6","metric":"rmse","shrinkage":0.0}

Thought: Test a weighted combination using the inverse‑error weights from pool6 (w9) to see if a simple weighted mean can beat the current median pool1 leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","weights":"w9","rationale":"inverse‑error weights on the top 3 models"}

Thought: Evaluate the meta‑model weights (w8) on the full pool to see if it beats the current leader.  
Action: evaluate_strategy  
Action Input: {"combine":"weighted","pool":"pool_full","weights":"w8","rationale":"test pooled meta‑model weights"}

